{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>When goods increase, those who consume them increase.</b> From the doubled conjugation [hifil], and it is a past-tense verb. He says: among verbs whose [middle] root letter is not whole, the imperative plural is like רבה צבאך וצאה." "<b>Yitron.</b> Like טוב וכשר (good and fitting). The matter is: after the goods that are his are eaten by many before him, what good is there for him in the goods? Only what his eyes see."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:43.896696570Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}